1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,680
Who here does not have a reliable way of getting customers?

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:04,680
As in like you get it all word of mouth predominantly.

3
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:07,560
Okay, one of the biggest mistakes that you make

4
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:08,840
from an acquisition perspective

5
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:11,200
is using a warm process on cold leads.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,320
The reverse always works and the inverse does not.

7
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:17,720
Meaning, if you use a warm process on cold leads,

8
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:19,800
you will not sell people and you will only sell

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,720
the six inch putts, which are the warm leads.

10
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:23,120
Which you pretty much could just be like,

11
00:00:23,120 --> 00:00:25,280
here's the price, buy it.

12
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,140
On the other hand, if you have a cold acquisition process,

13
00:00:28,140 --> 00:00:29,640
you can put a warm lead through it

14
00:00:29,800 --> 00:00:31,560
and they will buy at higher rates.

15
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:33,600
Who here was at the launch for the book?

16
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:38,320
At the launch, many people who were there knew who I was.

17
00:00:38,320 --> 00:00:41,040
There were also people there who did not know who I was.

18
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:42,360
The webinar was structured for people

19
00:00:42,360 --> 00:00:43,840
who had no idea who I was.

20
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:45,520
The people who did know were not offended.

21
00:00:45,520 --> 00:00:47,880
The people who didn't know were grateful to find out.

22
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:51,280
I could have probably sent an email with the offer

23
00:00:51,280 --> 00:00:53,080
and done a third of the sales we did.

24
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,800
The other two thirds came from actually selling

25
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:56,640
like we meant it.

